  "id": "social-loafing",
  "term": "social loafing",
  "definition": "Social loafing is the tendency for people to put in less personal effort when working on a group task than when their own contribution can be clearly identified. It is commonly discussed in group performance and teamwork, especially when responsibility is shared and individual effort is less visible.",
